	"name": "Nightwatch Cane",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/commodities/wood/wood-pole.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>In some particularly fashion-forward societies, it’s very common for the constabulary and even civilians to weild weaponized canes. From the ever popular sword cane to the shillelagh, they’re as much symbols of status as mobility aids or weapons. However, the nightwatch cane is notably different as it is not only built for melee use. Nightwatch canes come in two varieties, pistol or rifle.</p><p>A pistol nightwatch cane has a light firearm used as the hand-grip at the top of the cane. This allows one to simply shift their grip from the top of the pistol to the firing mechanism in order to shoot some burglar or ruffian in the street.</p><p>A rifle nightwatch cane uses the length of the cane itself as a light rifle. By lifting the cane into the off hand and raising it to shoulder height, one can look down the length of the cane to sight a target and fire a shot by pulling the firing mechanism in the handle.</p><p>Particularly advanced and expensive nightwatch canes may even have a revolving chamber, allowing up to 6 shots before reloading.</p>",
